   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**The typical reporting country's government spends about $21 per person a year on its heritage**, cultural and natural, using each country's latest figure from 2020–2024.\n\nSpending ranges widely: Belgium reported **$369 per person** (2023), Canada **$212** (2024) and Kenya **$4.18** (2024). Thirteen countries spent less than $1.\n\nOnly 74 countries report, so this is not a world average. Dollars are adjusted for price differences between countries. Source: UIS, February 2026 release.",
